# Opportunity Hunter — Connector Credentials Template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local runs (already gitignored — see
# repo root .gitignore), or set these as GitHub Actions repository
# secrets for production. Never fill in real values here and commit
# this file — it exists so the *names* are documented and version
# controlled, never the *values*.
#
# collect.py reads these automatically via os.environ and overlays
# them onto config/sources.json's committed placeholders at the start
# of every run (see collect.py's apply_env_overrides()) — the
# committed sources.json file itself should keep every value below as
# null/empty.
#
# See ../../CONNECTOR-CONFIGURATION-GUIDE.md for how to obtain each
# value.

# --- Upwork (OAuth2 + GraphQL) ---
# All three required together, or the connector cleanly skips.
UPWORK_API_KEY=
UPWORK_API_SECRET=
UPWORK_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# --- LinkedIn Jobs (Talent Solutions / Jobs API, partner access only) ---
LINKEDIN_JOBS_API_KEY=

# --- Wellfound (no known public/partner API yet) ---
# Set this only if/when Wellfound provides one and collectors/wellfound.py
# has been updated with the real implementation — see its docstring.
WELLFOUND_API_KEY=

# --- Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby ---
# These are public, unauthenticated APIs — the values below are
# company board tokens/slugs/job-board names, not secrets. They're
# listed here anyway so activation can be entirely environment-driven
# in production (no sources.json edit needed). Comma-separated, no
# spaces required around commas.
GREENHOUSE_BOARD_TOKENS=
LEVER_COMPANIES=
ASHBY_JOB_BOARD_NAMES=

# --- RemoteOK ---
# No configuration needed — this connector is already fully active.
